WEBVTT

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:05.640
Present Day

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:08.590
Present Time

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:23.340
And you don't seem to understand

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:28.540
A shame you seemed an honest man

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:33.290
And all the fears you hold so dear

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:38.560
Will turn to whisper in your ear

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:41.960
And you know what they say might hurt you

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:44.430
And you know that it means so much

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:49.190
And you don't even feel a thing

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:54.850
I am falling, I am fading

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:58.970
I have lost it all

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:26.990
I am falling, I am fading, I am drowning

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.630
Help me to breathe

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:34.840
I am hurting, I have lost it all

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:37.380
I am losing

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:41.580
Help me to breathe

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:12.230
Do you want to be hurt, too?

00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:16.230
Do you want your heart to feel like it's being scraped with a rasp?

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:20.870
If you do, don't look away, whatever you do.

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:41.210
Nobody knows if there is or not.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:47.020
It doesn't matter to the user if God exists in the Wired.

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:49.640
Just a second, Lain.

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:51.990
Let me take out this guy first.

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:58.670
What's so fun about this? All you do is kill other players.

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:04.860
Nobody knows what's fun and why.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:14.920
"Tachibana General Laboratories" was written on the door plate.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:29.670
A company as big as Tachibana General Labs wouldn't do anything illegal.

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:31.100
I've heard some rumors, though...

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:33.100
Rumors?

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:38.740
Do you know how we're able to exchange information in the Wired like this?

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:41.980
Oh, so you're testing me, huh?

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:44.910
You're talking about the IP.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:48.090
Sorry. You're right.

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:52.160
We aren't usually aware of the protocol's existence.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:58.000
But the current 6th-gen protocol has reached its data throughput limit.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:02.250
The 7th-gen protocol...

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:05.230
Yes. The 7th-gen protocol.

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:08.700
Big companies are the ones that're making it into the new infrastructure.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:14.180
To control the protocol is to control the economy of the Wired.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.620
I hear there's constant sabotage attempts going on.

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:20.020
And the party behind it is...

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:23.420
Tachibana General Labs.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.810
Sis?

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:02.330
Mom? Dad?

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:04.330
I...

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:11.800
A while ago, somebody asked me something.

00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:18.400
"Are you Iwakura Lain? Are your parents really your parents?"

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:22.100
Isn't that funny?

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:25.280
It's funny, isn't it?

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.640
People say the funniest things, huh?

00:06:29.730 --> 00:06:31.580
Right?

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:16.860
Good morning!

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:26.040
Arisu...

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:27.740
Good morning.

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:32.870
W-What's wrong?

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:40.020
I don't believe it, but...

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:43.750
W-What?

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:46.820
Lain, you didn't do it, right?

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:49.730
D-Didn't do what?

00:07:50.310 --> 00:07:52.230
She's just playing innocent!

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:54.930
Reika! You don't know that!

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:57.800
Lain, seriously. It wasn't you?

00:07:58.420 --> 00:08:01.240
What are you talking about?

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:05.160
Lain, in the Wired, did you...

00:08:12.070 --> 00:08:15.520
No, forget about it. It couldn't have been you, Lain.

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:21.060
I trust you. Okay?

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:23.510
Arisu!

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:49.880
Arisu!

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:29.500
It's too dangerous. Avoid approving any more bills.

00:09:29.950 --> 00:09:34.900
I can't believe it! How can such a nice guy be into such weird stuff?

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:37.910
There's an extremely serious bug in Protocol 6.

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:41.040
Damage caused by this may prove disastrous in the Wired.

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:44.250
Every night, a small, child-like person in a

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:46.450
red and green striped sweater appears in her room.

00:09:46.450 --> 00:09:49.600
When she was in high school, that pop singer hit someone

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:51.290
with her boyfriend's car and fled the scene!

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:54.520
It's gotta be true! I heard it firsthand!

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:58.230
That building's a famous haunted spot.

00:09:58.230 --> 00:09:59.470
If you look at a terminal at night,

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:02.230
internal e-mail shows up, but there's nobody there!

00:10:02.230 --> 00:10:05.200
The Knights don't exist! Some American students started it as a joke!

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:07.920
Shut up! Who cares about any of that?

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:11.370
Don't you find it interesting?

00:10:12.860 --> 00:10:14.200
Who's there?

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:18.840
You're looking for me, aren't you?

00:10:19.460 --> 00:10:21.520
So God makes His grand entrance, huh?

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:24.150
How do you define "God"?

00:10:24.150 --> 00:10:27.510
If it's the creator of the world, that's not me.

00:10:27.510 --> 00:10:32.780
The all-powerful ruler of the world? You give God too much credit.

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:34.560
Where are you?

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:40.690
But if you define God as one who exists everywhere in that other world?

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:45.600
If that's what you mean, then yes. I suppose you could call me that.

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:49.470
I have only a slight influence on the workings of the world, however.

00:10:49.470 --> 00:10:51.380
Who the hell are you?!

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:53.350
I am you.

00:10:53.350 --> 00:10:59.750
You must have realized that another you has always existed in the Wired.

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:04.120
You are merely a hologram of that other you.

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:06.560
You are just a body.

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:09.730
You expect me to believe that?

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:13.800
That's impossible. It's crazy.

00:11:15.220 --> 00:11:17.970
But you don't think that the you in the real world

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:22.000
is the same as the one standing here in the Wired, do you?

00:11:22.630 --> 00:11:25.840
But I'm me...

00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:59.210
Peeping Tom

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:07.450
Peeping Tom

00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:06.640
Arisu?

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:10.490
Arisu? Where are you?

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:12.190
Arisu?

00:13:12.190 --> 00:13:13.690
Arisu!

00:13:13.690 --> 00:13:15.260
Arisu! Where are you?

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:16.950
Arisu!

00:13:19.580 --> 00:13:23.290
Arisu, where are you? Arisu!

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:27.200
What did I do?

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:29.950
What did I do in the Wired?

00:13:30.550 --> 00:13:34.230
What's the other me doing?

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:48.400
Don't worry about the rumors! Don't worry about it!

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:42.770
Is it all right for you to do this with a teacher?

00:14:43.430 --> 00:14:45.750
N-No, it's not...

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:48.820
Why do it, then?

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:51.710
Because... I want to.

00:15:16.240 --> 00:15:22.250
"Hey, do you know who Mizuki Arisu likes?"

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:29.990
"Do you know who she's thinking of when she plays with herself?"

00:15:33.920 --> 00:15:37.910
It was you who told everyone! The rumors were true?!

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:41.190
Lain!

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:45.310
You've always been sitting there quietly, watching me?!

00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:50.370
You saw what I didn't want anybody to know! When I didn't want anybody to see!

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:51.910
And when I...

00:15:53.400 --> 00:15:55.470
Tell me it isn't true, Lain!

00:15:57.030 --> 00:15:58.220
Lain!

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:00.880
You...

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:50.540
Who are you?

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:54.150
You're not me.

00:16:54.920 --> 00:16:57.440
I'd never do what you do.

00:16:57.440 --> 00:16:59.380
I...

00:16:59.380 --> 00:17:04.580
Stop it! Why are you acting like the part of me that I hate?

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:14.800
You...

00:17:17.150 --> 00:17:20.260
I'm committing suicide!

00:17:24.150 --> 00:17:27.020
Why? Why are you warm?

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:31.520
Why do I have to feel your body heat?

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:35.520
Hey, I'm Lain, aren't I?

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:36.780
No!

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:38.280
No!

00:17:58.690 --> 00:18:00.720
What are these things?

00:18:01.820 --> 00:18:03.410
They're all you.

00:18:03.410 --> 00:18:07.010
I said that you've always existed in the Wired, didn't I?

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:09.740
You're the same as me.

00:18:09.740 --> 00:18:12.120
You're omnipresent in the Wired.

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:17.850
Wherever anyone is, wherever they go, you have always been there.

00:18:18.970 --> 00:18:22.560
You've watched what they didn't want others to see.

00:18:22.560 --> 00:18:24.950
You've told everyone about it, that's all.

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:28.040
It was the right thing to do.

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:32.500
The Wired's information should be shared, shouldn't it?

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:45.110
Everything you say is a lie.

00:18:45.110 --> 00:18:46.320
Why is that?

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:51.270
Arisu and the others said that they saw me in the Wired when I wasn't there.

00:18:51.270 --> 00:18:54.560
As long as I'm aware of myself,

00:18:54.560 --> 00:18:57.360
my true self is inside me!

00:18:59.620 --> 00:19:02.690
You're telling me that these dupes are me?

00:19:03.350 --> 00:19:05.320
What a load of garbage!

00:19:08.390 --> 00:19:10.030
I...

00:19:10.030 --> 00:19:13.110
If I'm really what you say I am, then...

00:19:14.030 --> 00:19:16.780
Then what, Lain?

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:22.760
Their memories of being seen by Lain... I could delete that information!

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:28.160
That's true. Give it a try.

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:32.390
You were born with that kind of power.

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:54.020
Good morning!

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:04.510
Lain!

00:20:07.010 --> 00:20:08.660
Hey, Lain!

00:20:11.620 --> 00:20:13.180
They forgot?

00:20:16.490 --> 00:20:18.440
They really forgot?

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:20.380
Lain!

00:20:23.100 --> 00:20:24.520
They did!

00:20:25.270 --> 00:20:26.610
Arisu!

00:20:30.140 --> 00:20:33.790
W-What?

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:35.290
Arisu!

00:20:36.680 --> 00:20:39.330
Hey, I wanna go to Cyberia today!

00:20:39.820 --> 00:20:41.030
C'mon, let's go!

00:20:41.620 --> 00:20:42.800
I second that!

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:44.970
Wow, this sure is unusual...

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:48.010
Sure. We can get changed at my place again and go from there.

00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:48.840
Great!

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:55.890
Hey, what should I wear?

00:20:56.240 --> 00:20:59.390
Stop it! I'm me!

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:08.240
I'm over here!

00:21:09.280 --> 00:21:10.140
Come on, hurry up!

00:21:10.140 --> 00:21:11.960
Hey, wait for me!

00:21:15.850 --> 00:21:20.870
That's right! Lain is Lain, and I'm me.

00:21:42.580 --> 00:21:44.190
Hello, Navi.

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:48.280
Hello, Lain.

00:21:55.360 --> 00:21:58.470
I... I'm me, right?

00:21:59.590 --> 00:22:03.980
There's no other me but me, right?

00:22:28.950 --> 00:22:33.380
nan no tsumi mo nai hazu na no ni

00:22:28.950 --> 00:22:33.380
Although I must be innocent,

00:22:33.380 --> 00:22:37.290
nanraka no batsu wo uketeru

00:22:33.380 --> 00:22:37.290
now I am punished.

00:22:37.720 --> 00:22:43.590
jibun de maita tane de mo nai no ni

00:22:37.720 --> 00:22:43.590
I wasn't the one who sowed those seeds, but nevertheless

00:22:44.310 --> 00:22:50.500
sakimidareta hana tsumasareru

00:22:44.310 --> 00:22:50.500
I have to pull up the flowers that bloomed from them.

00:22:57.050 --> 00:23:01.690
shiranai koto to mo ienai ga

00:22:57.050 --> 00:23:01.690
I can't say I didn't know about it,

00:23:01.690 --> 00:23:06.140
katabou katsuida oboe wa nai

00:23:01.690 --> 00:23:06.140
but I don't remember taking any part in it.

00:23:06.140 --> 00:23:12.330
jiyuu wo takaku kawasareta ki mo suru ga

00:23:06.140 --> 00:23:12.330
I think my freedom cost me dearly,

00:23:12.860 --> 00:23:19.570
kokoro made yasuku utta oboe wa nai

00:23:12.860 --> 00:23:19.570
but I don't remember selling my soul so cheaply.

00:23:19.930 --> 00:23:27.620
Hey Hey kutabatte osaraba suru made

00:23:19.930 --> 00:23:27.620
Hey hey, until I die and say farewell...

00:23:28.640 --> 00:23:37.530
Hey Hey dare no te ni mo kakaranai

00:23:28.640 --> 00:23:37.530
Hey hey... no one can touch me.

00:23:39.050 --> 00:23:43.140
tooi yoru wo urotsuiteiru

00:23:39.050 --> 00:23:43.140
You probably don't know

00:23:43.140 --> 00:23:50.850
shiranai darou eien no narazu monotachi wo

00:23:43.140 --> 00:23:50.850
the eternal outlaws prowling in the distant night.
